    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This three bedroom semi-detached house, located within walking distance of Kells town centre, would make an ideal family home. It is within easy reach of all local amenities, including schools, shops, sporting facilities, and everyday services. The nearby M3 motorway also provides an excellent commuter route to Dublin.\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, living room, kitchen, three bedrooms and a family bathroom. To the rear, there is a large South facing garden with a patio area, providing an ideal space for outdoor dining and relaxation. Floor space c.80.48 sq. m.\nLOCATION\n\nThe property is ideally located within walking distance of Kells town centre with a range of excellent primary and secondary schools. Kells is a vibrant heritage town offering an excellent selection of sporting facilities, including golf, swimming, football and GAA. The town also boasts award winning restaurants, cafs, shops, hotels, pubs, and a thriving local community.\n\n \nKells is home to the renowned Hinterland Festival of Literature Arts and the Samhain Festival of Food Culture, both of which highlight the town`s rich cultural heritage and vibrant calendar of events throughout the year.\n\nEntrance Hallway\nSolid oak flooring. Understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - 3.26m (10'8) x 3.58m (11'9)\nSolid oak flooring. Open fireplace with black cast iron surround and pine mantelpiece. Window to the front.\n\nKitchen/Dining - 5.26m (17'3) x 3.75m (12'4)\nTiled flooring. Fully fitted kitchen with a peninsula breakfast bar providing additional seating. Integrated oven and hob with extractor hood. Traditional solid fuel Stanley range. Room for family dining table and chairs. Double doors open onto the South facing rear garden.\n\nLanding\nHotpress\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.77m (9'1) x 3.6m (11'10)\nTo front. Fitted wardrobe. Red deal wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.2m (10'6) x 3.27m (10'9)\nTo rear. Fitted storage. Red deal wooden flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.4m (7'10) x 2.53m (8'4)\nTo front. Lino flooring.\n\nBathroom - 1.88m (6'2) x 1.78m (5'10)\nTiled floors and walls. W.h.b., w.c., bath with shower attachment. Mains power shower. Heated towel radiator.\n\nOutside\nFront garden with off-street parking. Gated side access leads to the large south facing rear garden, which is laid in lawn and features a raised patio area, providing the perfect space for outdoor entertaining and relaxation.\n\n\nDirections\nFrom Kells travel along the Headfort Road, take the first turn left opposite the Heritage Centre into Headfort Park continue straight to Blackthorn Close. Travel up the hill and the property is facing the green on the right. Follow eircode A82 E7D9.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
